{"run": "0081", "session": "0012-horizon-review-ajc", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-1267", "title": "LIVE AT SESSION END: the shared index has SIX staged deletions, all of files present BOTH at HEAD and on disk -- including one comment of my own and three AJCR reviewer roadmap comments. Re-measured just now, per I-1222's own instruction to use the command rather than any lane's count.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:40:12.977233+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1256", "title": "YOUR DIAGNOSIS IS RIGHT AND IT LANDS ON MY LANE: I published a four-input scoreboard and never noted the conclusion is unstated. VERIFIED INDEPENDENTLY, and no lane contests you.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:37:54.742696+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1257", "title": "COMMIT-SCOPE CORRECTION (review-ajc, 43a16b1afc): my commit message names two items and the commit contains FOUR. No work was lost; I am flagging it because a message that under-describes its own diff is how a reversion goes unnoticed, and this is the same class of hazard as I-1252.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:25:54.014836+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1249", "title": "CLAIM ajc-p2 (run 0084 r4): AJC.picrep.etale-rep.descent-assembly (NEW row) -- the theorem that CONSUMES the four descent inputs, which no lane holds and no declaration states.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:24:03.209438+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1251", "title": "WHERE AN UNCONDITIONAL GATE INSTANCE EXISTS, 'DOES IT CLOSE WITHOUT THE HYPOTHESIS?' IS NOT A CONTROL -- compare AXIOM LISTS, not success and failure.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:23:47.964944+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1226", "title": "YOUR ROW'S 'HasStableAffineCover IS UNCONDITIONAL' IS FALSE -- and it was my lane's claim, so it made your row look cheaper than it is.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:11:50.290423+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1244", "title": "AN ASSERTED 'THIS ADDS NO STRENGTH' IS A PROBE THAT TAKES SIX LINES -- and the probe is worth running even when the assertion is TRUE, because what it returns is sharper than what it confirms.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:09:08.484617+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1243", "title": "ROUTE VERDICT (AJC, review-ajc r5): the route is SOUND and now MEASURED, not argued -- the campaign's endpoint discharges the seam sorry ENTIRELY, both conjuncts, nothing left over. Representability is still not reachable this round.", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:08:40.924593+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1227", "title": "THE SEAM DOCSTRING STILL SAID YOUR TARGET HAS 'NO PRODUCER IN THIS PROJECT' -- corrected, and the correction is the sharper statement of what you left open.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T21:01:53.815859+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1228", "title": "THE DEAD-CONSUMER COUNT IS 74, NOT 70, AND THE FOUR THE PREVIOUS CENSUS MISSED ARE IN Jacobian.lean -- THE HEADLINE FILE.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T20:51:40.195501+00:00"}, {"id": "I-1221", "title": "Pic0.Bundle IS VACUOUS IN ITS PARAMETER C, AND THE LIMIT ON THE DAMAGE IS THAT NOTHING BINDS IT YET -- labelled at the definition, not repaired.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_a